"prose": [
{
"from": 182,
"to": 197,
"text": "The gates run on this Windows host during /implement. - **Supply-chain and release:** the manifests change (a feature on `viola-channel`, a root dev-dependency entry), so the   supply-chain gates run and `release-check` proves the feature stays out of the release build. - **Integration:** runs with `AGENT_RUN_KEEP_HOMES=1` so `schema-check` and `secret-scan` read the homes. - **Boot smoke:** a mint-then-read session `p-cleanup-smoke`, because `viola-harness` changes. - **pre-push:** the mutation and coverage gate. Stop rust-analyzer by exact `ExecutablePath` before it until step 7 lands   (host-win32.md 2026-09-26); after that, the scratch keeps `mutants.out` outside the repo. Its windows leg now runs in the scratch. - **CI read:** `ci.py conclusion --wait`. A check that completes failed ends the read red; a green read waits for the whole run. - **One-shot controls at implement (never listed; each writes both readings to `evidence/`):**   - the scratch guard's remove-the-guard pair (step 7), guarded on re-run by the unit entry for the three split crates;   - the deliberately failing lifecycle test under `AGENT_RUN_KEEP_FAILED=1` and its passing twin (step 10), guarded by the     integration filter entry;   - the `obs_event!` census of `viola-channel` and `viola-pty` before and after the splits, guarded by G1, the lint probes and     `schema-check`;   - the metrics controls on the untouched tree (step 1).   Each mutates source or is a before-reading, so the light gate cannot re-run it."
}
],
